  <h2>The problem we exist to fix</h2>
  <p>
    Commercial roofing decisions are expensive, infrequent, and asymmetrical. The people
    making them — owners, boards, managers — face them a handful of times in a career.
    The people selling to them face them every day. Almost all available information is
    published by someone with something to sell.
  </p>
  <p>
    The result is predictable: premature replacements, mismatched systems, voided
    warranties, under-documented insurance claims, and millions of dollars in avoidable
    cost — not because anyone lied, but because no neutral reference existed.
  </p>

  <h2>Our mission</h2>
  <p>
    We build the neutral reference. CRI publishes evidence-based knowledge, transparent
    decision tools, and proprietary research so that every commercial roofing decision can
    be made on evidence rather than sales pressure.
  </p>

  <h2>Our principles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Accuracy before speed.</strong> We publish when the work is verified, not when the calendar says so.</li>
    <li><strong>Trust before traffic.</strong> We optimize for being right, cited, and returned to — not for clicks.</li>
    <li><strong>Education before selling.</strong> Every page must help the reader decide, whether or not that decision ever benefits us.</li>
    <li><strong>Evidence, always.</strong> We never fabricate. Where evidence is uncertain, we say so plainly.</li>
    <li><strong>Long-term reputation before short-term revenue.</strong> We think in decades.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What success looks like</h2>
  <p>
    Success is a facility manager checking CRI before a contractor meeting, an HOA board
    citing a CRI dataset in a reserve study, an adjuster and an owner using the same CRI
    reference page — and all of them trusting it because our standards are public and our
    incentives are disclosed.
  </p>
</GovernanceLayout>
